4. lab16r — THE THREE BRANCH-REF READS COMPOSE ACROSS A REAL REBASE
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Not asked for; it is the interaction the three reads newly create. lab16's
shape plus a trunk commit under the branch, strategy rebase, so
`sourceExcludeDirs` is evaluated AFTER `rebaseOntoTrunk` rewrote `branch`.
  merge -> "opus/W-001 was rebased onto master — ... certifies
            tree:d819baa2..., which no longer matches the rebased tree
            (tree:9c6922f5...)"                              exit 1
That refusal is CORRECT: the rebase genuinely pulled a new source file in.
Remedy verbatim -> verify certifies tree:9c6922f5 (computed under the
branch's own exclude set, post-rewrite), commit, retry ->
  "merged opus/W-001 into master"                            exit 0
`git show <branch>:...` reads the rewritten branch, so the exclude set and
the hash it defines stay in step through the rewrite. One pass, no loop.

