WHY I AM PASSING THIS, EXACTLY
-------------------------------
Not "the tests are green". Three things, and each is a thing I ran:

(1) The converging sequence closed on the function I named. At round 7 I
wrote that every blocking finding in rounds 5-7 was one bug — a read
pointing at the checkout instead of the branch ref — and that the
implementation was one function short of obeying its own rule. The diff
since round 7 is exactly that one function and nothing else; I diffed it
literally. The prediction was falsifiable and it held.

(2) I reproduced the defect and its absence on ONE frozen repository state,
swapping only branch.ts. Pre-fix: the refusal, the byte-identical
re-verification, the "nothing to commit", the identical refusal on retry.
Post-fix, same commits: exit 0, branch deleted. That is a controlled
experiment, not a passing test.

(3) `merge`'s compare path now has no disk read left in it. `readOpusRecord`
(certificates and state) and `sourceExcludeDirs` (the exclude set that
defines the hash both are compared against) both read `git show
<branch>:<studio-rel>/...`, with the same fallback and the same parse. I
mutated the new read two ways — forced to the disk fallback, and pointed at
HEAD — and behaviour 31 caught both in all three assertions. And I checked
the reads compose: lab8 (fail-open) still refuses, lab11 (waived) still
merges, lab16r shows the exclude set tracking the branch through a real
rebase rewrite. Three reads, one provenance, no regression between them.

On the design question the brief asks: the design of putting certificate
checking inside `merge` is sound and is now correctly implemented. The
sequence converged; it did not stall. I have no blocking finding this round.

Advisories
----------
A8.1  M-X3 (dropping `sourceExcludeDirs`'s disk fallback entirely) causes 0
      FAIL — the studio-outside-repo path is unpinned, as round 4's A4.4
      already found for the pre-B7.1 version of this function and behaviour
      22 only partly closed. It fails CLOSED (losing `source_excludes` means
      a larger hash, so merge refuses rather than lands), so this is a
      coverage gap, not a hole. Worth one assertion, not a round.
A8.2  `resolveIntegration` still reads bisellium.yml off DISK while
      `sourceExcludeDirs` now reads the SAME FILE from the branch — round 7
      flagged this as untested, so I tested it (labint): an opus whose own
      work is adopting `integration: strategy: rebase` has that declaration
      ignored, because merge uses the trunk's (absent) block and falls back
      to fast_forward -> "branch opus/W-001 has diverged from master —
      rebase first". Clearable in two documented steps (manual rebase, then
      the stale-certificate remedy), so advisory, not blocking. I think the
      split is actually DEFENSIBLE — `integration:` is the officina's merge
      policy, an operator/checkout property, while `source_excludes` is an
      input to the artifact's own hash — but nothing says so anywhere, and
      ADOPTION.md's new paragraph ("read the same way too") invites the
      reader to assume the whole manifest follows the branch. One sentence
      in ADOPTION.md, or a follow-up opus if the policy should follow the
      branch after all.
A8.3  Carried from A7.5, still open: behaviours 29 and 30 are labelled
      "pre-implementation" in the brief but are partial reds (one genuinely
      new assertion each; the logs themselves are honest and show the PASS
